WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.234
Atoms bond together to become more stable,

00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:06.028
usually by getting a full outer shell of

00:00:06.028 --> 00:00:06.727
electrons.

00:00:06.727 --> 00:00:09.242
There are two main types of chemical

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.058
bonds: ionic and covalent.

00:00:11.058 --> 00:00:13.992
We'll explore how they form and what makes

00:00:13.992 --> 00:00:15.040
them different.

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:17.368
In ionic bonding,

00:00:17.368 --> 00:00:20.353
electrons are transferred from a metal

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:22.316
atom to a non-metal atom.

00:00:22.316 --> 00:00:24.830
For example, in sodium chloride,

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:27.736
sodium (a metal) gives an electron to

00:00:27.736 --> 00:00:29.542
chlorine (a non-metal).

00:00:29.542 --> 00:00:32.684
Both atoms become stable with full outer

00:00:32.684 --> 00:00:33.233
shells.

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:36.569
When sodium loses an electron,

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:38.594
it becomes a positive ion.

00:00:38.594 --> 00:00:41.708
Chlorine gains an electron and becomes a

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:42.721
negative ion.

00:00:42.721 --> 00:00:45.991
These resulting ions have opposite charges

00:00:45.991 --> 00:00:48.482
and attract each other strongly,

00:00:48.482 --> 00:00:50.273
forming the ionic bond.

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:52.824
In covalent bonding,

00:00:52.824 --> 00:00:55.783
electrons are shared between non-metal

00:00:55.783 --> 00:00:56.250
atoms.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.819
For instance, two chlorine atoms,

00:00:58.819 --> 00:01:00.065
both non-metals,

00:01:00.065 --> 00:01:02.090
share a pair of electrons.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:05.360
This sharing allows each atom to achieve a

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:07.307
stable, full outer shell.

00:01:08.333 --> 00:01:11.363
Both ionic and covalent bonds help atoms

00:01:11.363 --> 00:01:14.316
achieve stable electron configurations,

00:01:14.316 --> 00:01:16.361
but they do it differently.

00:01:16.361 --> 00:01:19.542
Ionic bonds involve a complete transfer of

00:01:19.542 --> 00:01:20.299
electrons,

00:01:20.299 --> 00:01:23.329
while covalent bonds involve the sharing

00:01:23.329 --> 00:01:25.373
of electrons between atoms.

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:27.024
Remember,

00:01:27.024 --> 00:01:29.579
ionic bonds form when electrons are

00:01:29.579 --> 00:01:30.455
transferred,

00:01:30.455 --> 00:01:33.011
creating charged ions that attract.

00:01:33.011 --> 00:01:35.786
Covalent bonds form when electrons are

00:01:35.786 --> 00:01:37.319
shared between atoms.

00:01:37.319 --> 00:01:40.312
Both methods allow atoms to reach stable,

00:01:40.312 --> 00:01:41.627
full outer shells.
